<BaseLayout title="Editorial policy"><div class="wrap static-page"><span class="eyebrow">Trust & learning</span><h1>How we tell these stories.</h1><div class="prose">
<h2>Clarity over certainty</h2><p>We aim to make complex subjects approachable without pretending that a tradition has only one history or that all communities celebrate the same way. We distinguish historical scholarship from folklore and modern interpretation.</p>
<h2>Sources and attribution</h2><p>Educational articles link to further sources when available. We write original summaries and respect the rights of authors, artists and translators. We do not host unauthorized book copies.</p>
<h2>Corrections</h2><p>We review substantive issues before revising articles. This project is still establishing a public contact channel and editorial review process, so please consider these pages a developing educational collection rather than an encyclopedia.</p>
<h2>Event listings</h2><p>We only intend to list events with verified organizer information, dates and official registration links. Events are not endorsements by the project.</p>
</div></div></BaseLayout>
